1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
I need a score better outside of classic lit.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Won't be able to get a doctor's note for the quiz.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Too bad quiz allergies aren't real.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Kutatsu study party?

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Exams are almost here.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Looks cozy. How's about a join you kiddos?

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Go away.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Um, there actually isn't room for you.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Just Sota, Miyamura, Mom, and me. That's it.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
You know, you treat me worse by the day.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
I'm gonna cry.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
I found this to be a genius.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Maybe later, he sa你说 it didn't be better now.

14
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Mainly, no normals is really good.

15
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,000
A last strived sting, however,

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,000
But this might have gone insane.

17
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Come, your sis is a voter.

18
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,820
Like you, your VAS

19
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
This is your fourth star's life.

20
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:23,980
Thank you.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:53,980
Thank you.

22
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:23,980
Thank you.

23
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:53,980
Thank you.

24
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,240
I'm just calling and I would really like to answer.

25
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,400
Answer where you are.

26
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:00,000
I am not letting the carpet.

27
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,300
Whoa.

28
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,580
I guess I dozed off.

29
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:04,800
That's like 10.

30
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,960
Keep it down, Kiyoko.

31
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,480
I wonder if you didn't bridge my life with every move you make.

32
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,440
Oh, you're being ridiculous, but what else is new?

33
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:13,440
Right, Miyamoto?

34
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:14,880
Wait, what's wrong?

35
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,760
I need to take a leak.

36
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,400
Oh, but I should wake Sota first.

37
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,240
I get sick if he sleeps here all night.

38
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:22,400
Hey, little buddy.

39
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:23,420
Whoa!

40
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:26,780
You're twisting my leg, funny, and I got it!

41
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:28,200
Tell you, quit moving, Kiyosuke!

42
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:33,280
We created a world where we endlessly wound each other.

43
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,300
Should we call for help or simply pray?

44
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:40,940
Calling for help would be too embarrassing since we're all tangled up like a pose from some edgy manga.

45
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,500
Aren't we, Miyamoto?

46
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,780
It's about to break!

47
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,320
Kiyosuke, why are you here?

48
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,440
Things were fine till your stupid self joined in!

49
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,560
Well, excuse me.

50
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,440
If I could get out, I already would have.

51
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:51,700
I'm done.

52
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:54,160
My body's paralyzed by the need for a bathroom.

53
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,780
It's up to you guys now.

54
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,220
Don't you dare call it quits!

55
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:58,960
Let's assess the dilemma.

56
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:01,240
One of us must be sacrificed.

57
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:02,180
All right.

58
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,080
I can try and yank my way free.

59
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:05,380
Wait, time out.

60
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,580
Kiyosuke's right leg is currently trapped between my legs.

61
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,320
Hori's are also wrapped pretty tightly around me.

62
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:15,240
Pulling will only cause excruciating pain before ultimately failing.

63
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:16,380
Valid points.

64
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:17,600
Then what's the plan?

65
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:21,440
You two bite the bullet while I tear my way out of here.

66
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:22,500
Hold it, Buster!

67
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,060
Just what kind of anti-autic idea is that?

68
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:28,340
If someone needs to rescue more than me, speak now or forever hold your pain!

69
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,440
I am uncomfortable too.

70
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,640
My skirt flip, but you don't hear me whining, do you?

71
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:32,380
What?

72
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,580
How's that even an issue?

73
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,320
You're hidden!

74
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:37,020
Don't go back to sleep!

75
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:38,760
Oh, man.

76
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:41,060
Maybe we shouldn't have had and drunk all that tea about now.

77
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,180
Hey, wait.

78
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:44,080
There.

79
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:46,240
If I do that, then...

80
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:48,780
Holy stinkin' crap!

81
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,620
It's actually free!

82
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:50,160
It is?

83
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:50,980
That's great!

84
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:53,260
I got one out too!

85
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:55,280
Rise and shine, sleeping ugly!

86
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:57,520
Freedom is mine!

87
00:04:57,520 --> 00:05:03,740
What do you think?

88
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:04,880
You make it in time?

89
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,980
I think I'm just glad the crisis has ended.

90
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:12,200
Just spitballing?

91
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:17,380
But instead of lying down in three different directions, let's try facing the same way.

92
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:18,800
Yeah, okay.

93
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:28,200
I woke up well after dark the last time I was here.

94
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,540
So I'll head home around seven today.

95
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,520
Which gives us about an hour.

96
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,200
Just enough time for a nap.

97
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,000
Don't even play.

98
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:48,280
Hey, aren't you Sengoku's boy?

99
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:50,140
Huh?

100
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:51,980
Remember me?

101
00:05:52,220 --> 00:05:55,120
Used to come over to our house and play all the time when you were little.

102
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,340
Kyo-chan's dad?

103
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:57,860
Yeah, I remember.

104
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,460
Dang, you sure grew up!

105
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,180
Well, you are Kyo-ko's age, right?

106
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:05,360
Puberty at work.

107
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:08,120
Man, that's it.

108
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,060
Listen, Kakiru.

109
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,820
The horis are bad news.

110
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:12,460
Have been ever since high school.

111
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,860
Hold your ground or they'll lead you by the nose and that's all she wrote!

112
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,360
Wait, that's all who wrote?

113
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,180
I'm just telling you they're trouble!

114
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:20,580
So, Kat!

115
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:21,900
I mean, Takiru.

116
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,080
How's your old man been doing?

117
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,400
My name's Kakiru!

118
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:26,300
And my dad's doing well, thank you.

119
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:27,860
Yeah.

120
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:30,000
He's doing well, is he?

121
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:32,900
Something tells me he wants to change that!

122
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:37,260
Pardon me, sir, but I was on my way home from buying erasers.

123
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:41,060
Ah, stop by our place for a visit while you're in the area.

124
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:44,240
Come warm yourself up before you start trekking back to your house!

125
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:58,860
Hey, tall, dumb, and lazy.

126
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:01,600
You had to wait until I'd just fallen asleep.

127
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,600
When did Sengoku get here?

128
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:04,600
And how?

129
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:10,840
Duh, he walked, ran into him around nine o'clock, brought him over, and then in the middle

130
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,960
of our chat, we both got really sleepy.

131
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:15,420
Miyamorta, it's midnight already.

132
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:16,820
Huh?

133
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:17,780
Oh.

134
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:19,840
Save it.

135
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,080
Always save before you go in dungeons.

136
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:23,060
Huh?

137
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:25,040
Mr. President knows.

138
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,400
Forget it, save's like the worst ever.

139
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:32,720
Yeah, but before that, buy magic recovery items while you're in town.

140
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:33,260
Yeah.

141
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:36,220
A surprise monster encounter, ah!

142
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:36,760
AHHHHH!

143
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:37,840
What?

144
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:38,340
No!

145
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:39,840
How'd that golem get here?

146
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,460
Was that directed at me?

147
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:42,380
Calm down!

148
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:44,760
I'm the quick quirk of the beast with the destruction spell!

149
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,940
How about you calm down?

150
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,400
Yay, we're saved!

151
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,340
The heroes are here!

152
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,480
You stay out of this!

153
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:50,320
Why?

154
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,140
Is the press here, or am I dreaming?

155
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:53,880
I was abducted nearby.

156
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:55,460
Kiyosuke's doing.

157
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,660
I haven't had a bath or eaten dinner.

158
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:00,760
Just plopped down and passed out.

159
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,540
I still gotta wash up, too.

160
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:03,680
We have a tub.

161
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,680
Go take your baths together for all I care.

162
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:08,640
Hori, there's kinda sorta something that he shouldn't see?

163
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:11,180
What, like a secret birthmark, or...?

164
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:11,820
Oh, nothing!

165
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:17,040
Oh, I just remembered that during our school trip!

166
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,040
You waited till late to use the public baths!

167
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,380
I can't seem to recall.

168
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,980
You wouldn't get in the pool, either.

169
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:23,780
I could never understand why.

170
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:27,440
Um, well, you see, I'm all skin and bone!

171
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:32,180
If you're categorized as skin and bone, I'm already dead.

172
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,400
Hey, stop!

173
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,320
That wasn't supposed to be any form of money!

174
00:08:37,320 --> 00:09:00,760
Uh-oh.

175
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:03,560
Looks like we succumbed yet again.

176
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,160
This kotatsu is dangerous.

177
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:07,860
Wake up, Miyamura!

178
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,880
Come on, don't leave your phone open.

179
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,480
Text piling up?

180
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:20,240
I guess I sent those last texts to Miyamura on accident.

181
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:22,560
Ah, so that's why Chika hasn't shown.

182
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,200
Where are you?

183
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:26,520
I know it's been cold lately and all, but I'd like to apologize for what happened the other day.

184
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:27,720
Can you come to the partner's school?

185
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,060
I'll be waiting at our usual spot.

186
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,180
You can say whatever you like, and I promise I'll still love you, even though I don't say it much.

187
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:33,220
I know you'll understand.

188
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:36,460
I'll still love you!

189
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:38,980
Wake up!

190
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,000
I want an explanation!

191
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:44,820
Shindo, your voice is annoying as ever.

192
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:48,620
Huh?

193
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:53,200
Feels like someone smashed their fist into my forehead with every ounce of strength they had.

194
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,440
Nah, must have imagined it.

195
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:58,060
Ahori?

196
00:09:59,000 --> 00:09:59,660
You asleep?

197
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:03,140
Oh, just faking?

198
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:04,940
Well, you might want to stop.

199
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:06,000
It's eight o'clock.

200
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,560
I'm aware of that.

201
00:10:08,020 --> 00:10:09,160
You're angry, aren't you?

202
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:10,040
But why?

203
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,100
The world may never know.

204
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,460
I'm not angry!

205
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:15,100
Really?

206
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,120
Don't make me repeat myself!

207
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:19,880
Hey, looky here!

208
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,600
We've got some mandarins, your favorite.

209
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:24,580
I'll peel one for you.

210
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:25,140
Hm?

211
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:34,560
Wow.

212
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,800
That actually got her up?

213
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,160
Don't laugh.

214
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:41,020
Oh, that's right!

215
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:43,440
I made myself a promise that I would only eat two a day!

216
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,840
So you hate them now?

217
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:45,580
What gives?

218
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:47,800
I don't like mandarin-flavored things.

219
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:49,700
Same with yuzu, citron, and grapefruit.

220
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:50,400
All the citrus!

221
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:53,380
I can't even bear to look at it!

222
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,620
Ohori, but it's peeled and ready to go.

223
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:57,680
Come on.

224
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:58,780
Get it away!

225
00:10:58,900 --> 00:10:59,440
One slice.

226
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:00,040
What's the harm?

227
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:00,540
Eat it!

228
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:04,080
I'm gonna kiss you if you don't eat it.

229
00:11:07,260 --> 00:11:08,720
I'll also kiss you if you do.

230
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:16,340
Good.

231
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:17,460
The storm has passed.

232
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,340
You're not mad anymore.

233
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,680
So that's what he was trying to do.

234
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,680
There was a text that said...

235
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:34,680
He keeps feeding me things like this.

236
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,940
Is it out of habit?

237
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:39,960
Want some candy?

238
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:41,120
Here.

239
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:43,460
No!

240
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:48,360
I will not stand for that.

241
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:49,260
Huh.

242
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:50,860
It's like clockwork, I swear.

243
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:58,020
That's from our grade school camping trip.

244
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:01,340
I didn't expect to find pictures like this here at your place, dude.

245
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,580
Well, we kind of grew up together and all.

246
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,160
You haven't changed a bit.

247
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:06,500
Except for, like, your height.

248
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:08,940
Oh, you think so?

249
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:10,380
That album.

250
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:11,900
It has pictures we haven't seen?

251
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,120
Give it here.

252
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:15,200
Oh, it's nothing worth seeing.

253
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:16,420
Pretty boring, really.

254
00:12:17,060 --> 00:12:17,800
What's in there?

255
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,680
Do you see anything good?

256
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:20,120
Why don't we play some games, Miyamura?

257
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,940
We've still got no Super Nintendo!

258
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,300
Put the album down and let us go!

259
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:29,720
12-year-old Sengaku screwed up cutting his hair.

260
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:32,120
I've got to see that kind of go to my own eyes!

261
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:33,340
You guys want me to die from there?

262
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:34,620
Man, this is too funny.

263
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:36,020
This is a few times, Freddy.

264
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,080
Put the jerks!

265
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:44,660
You're a lonely con.

266
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,940
No, I am not, I swear!

267
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,700
So, if three's as low as you go,

268
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,980
what's the max age before your interest goes out the window?

269
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:51,980
I don't go lower than high school,

270
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,160
so let's drop this joke.

271
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:56,240
Kyochan still changes clothes

272
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,760
in front of other people to this day.

273
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,420
I'm pretty sure zero high school girls

274
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:04,560
change clothes with an audience.

275
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:05,480
That includes Hori.

276
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,860
Oh, but she did it fairly recently,

277
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,620
and I was there.

278
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,100
I have gym first period today!

279
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:14,540
I'm borrowing this room for like five minutes, okay?

280
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:15,700
Sure, whatever.

281
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:18,120
I don't have time to go to the locker room.

282
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:22,620
Kyochan, you're not self-conscious at all, are you?

283
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:24,540
Even though I haven't moved.

284
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:25,200
And?

285
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:28,220
If I'm being honest, I could still use the toilet

286
00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:29,820
or take a bath with you in the same room.

287
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,080
So what?

288
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,220
She thinks so little of it.

289
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,780
He might as well be a fly on the wall.

290
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,680
I found her rationale very strange,

291
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:39,080
so I asked if she would strip in front of Miyamura, too.

292
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:40,700
And she said...

293
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:43,940
No, never in a million years!

294
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:45,860
Rather aggressively.

295
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:47,360
Oh, I see.

296
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:48,780
Sorry, I guess.

297
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,400
I suppose we did take baths together

298
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,260
all the time when we were little kids.

299
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:55,080
Well, as kids, sure.

300
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:58,940
Wait, what age did we stop that?

301
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:04,100
I feel like it dragged on

302
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,800
for an inappropriately long time.

303
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,440
I'm scared to remember.

304
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,180
Kindergarten or so?

305
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,100
Yeah, that sounds right.

306
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,960
Maybe first grade, but not past that.

307
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:14,160
I can't say it.

308
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:15,620
Makes sense.

309
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:16,220
Yeah.

310
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:21,440
Baron Stock!

311
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:23,860
Sota said he really likes these,

312
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,100
so I want to give him a try.

313
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:28,100
I'll go and check out.

314
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,320
Gosh, I am so sorry.

315
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:35,540
Thank you.

316
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,200
Aren't you Koyanagi?

317
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:38,860
No, sir.

318
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:39,640
You're mistaken.

319
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:44,060
Sengoku?

320
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:46,480
Wait.

321
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,800
Would you happen to be Hori's daughter?

322
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:49,720
Yeah!

323
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:51,800
And you must be Sengoku's father!

324
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,740
Kakaru is always helping.

325
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:55,400
He's just such a good boy.

326
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,600
Kind of you to say.

327
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,060
So you're the president's father?

328
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:01,600
It's nice to meet you.

329
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:02,120
I'm Miyamura.

330
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,260
Your son and I have become

331
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:05,360
really great friends.

332
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:08,180
What a difference!

333
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,360
You mustn't be corrupted

334
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:10,660
by the Hori family, okay?

335
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:11,140
Huh?

336
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:13,900
You know, I'm standing within earshot.

337
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,500
His dad seems nice.

338
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:19,760
I think I'm a fan.

339
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,000
Kakaru's like his clone.

340
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,080
We were looking at the future president

341
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:24,560
in a way.

342
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:27,020
But why did he call you Koyanagi?

343
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,420
Oh, that's my mom's maiden name.

344
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:31,140
My parents went to the same high school

345
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:32,140
as Sengoku's dad,

346
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:33,000
so they've known each other

347
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,740
for, like, ever.

348
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:34,680
Hmm.

349
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:37,980
I wonder what they were like back then.

350
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:40,340
Hey, how would you describe

351
00:15:40,340 --> 00:15:41,240
your parents, huh?

352
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:42,220
My folks?

353
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:43,720
Hmm.

354
00:15:44,020 --> 00:15:44,460
Normal?

355
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,340
Well, I guess that's one more thing

356
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:47,460
we have in common, then.

357
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:47,820
Huh?

358
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:51,300
How could you drop it

359
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:52,500
when you would half-laugh, dummy?

360
00:15:52,500 --> 00:16:06,960
You guys, uh...

361
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:08,400
remain a very few words, huh?

362
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:10,340
It's not that we're staying quiet.

363
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:11,980
The conversation just keeps dying.

364
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,660
Help me explain how terrible

365
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:14,580
he is at this, Kakaru.

366
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,680
I'm not terrible at anything.

367
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,280
I was simply reminiscing

368
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,620
about the good old days.

369
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:20,780
Ain't that right, right?

370
00:16:20,780 --> 00:16:22,200
Uh, sure.

371
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,580
You can be honest.

372
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:25,280
In fact, you should be honest.

373
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:26,040
There you go.

374
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,460
Brushing off someone's opinion

375
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:28,200
because you don't like...

376
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:28,860
I hate it here.

377
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:30,000
It's been cold outside!

378
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,380
Whoa, now there's a face

379
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:33,200
I didn't expect.

380
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:34,900
Welcome back!

381
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:35,800
Is Dad's here, too?

382
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,340
Ah, the pleasant one.

383
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:38,660
Hurry in and warm up.

384
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:44,420
Hey!

385
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,460
Why did you two decide to blink me?

386
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,960
You realize there's more room

387
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,860
on the other side?

388
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:50,400
It's cold over by the window,

389
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:50,980
so deal.

390
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:52,980
Now, can you please explain

391
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:53,840
why you and your dad

392
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:54,500
are even here?

393
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,020
Your father ran into mine

394
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,220
coming home from work.

395
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,660
I happened to be there, too,

396
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,820
and he abducted us both.

397
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:00,600
Does getting kidnapped

398
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,020
run on your family, or what?

399
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,100
You're thin enough

400
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:04,160
that I can feel a giraffe

401
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,420
blowing right through you, Prez.

402
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,240
I apologize.

403
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:08,760
You live here, too.

404
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:09,820
Seems like it.

405
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:11,260
You waltzed in so casually

406
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:12,620
one could only assume you do.

407
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:14,500
Well, kind of.

408
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:16,280
Believe it or not,

409
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,260
he's dating Gyoko.

410
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,660
They're such a cute couple.

411
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,000
Ah.

412
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:22,340
Well, Kakeru has no time

413
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:23,940
for dating or silly school drama.

414
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:24,540
What?

415
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:26,200
Not that it's wrong, mind you.

416
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:27,500
My son just doesn't need

417
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:28,200
a love interest.

418
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:29,540
It would interfere

419
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:30,300
with his studies.

420
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:35,880
So, is he joking with us?

421
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,300
Or have you been lying?

422
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:38,140
I wouldn't call it

423
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,020
outright lying.

424
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,360
I just haven't gotten around

425
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,300
to telling him the truth.

426
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,300
I thought I'd force an opportunity

427
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:44,600
by inviting Remy over

428
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,200
on Christmas, but...

429
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:47,580
I wanted to be in my room!

430
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,400
I wound up going

431
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,640
to her place instead.

432
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:53,320
I was surrounded by insects.

433
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:54,640
Yikes.

434
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:55,760
Though, I've kept quiet

435
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:56,220
till now.

436
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,320
I do intend to tell him.

437
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:58,320
Uh...

438
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:02,540
Are you cold, President?

439
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:03,660
The way you're shaking

440
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:04,380
is concerning.

441
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,420
Don't you say a word.

442
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:07,640
Oh, and what word

443
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,240
would that be?

444
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:09,620
What's up?

445
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,440
Playing a word game?

446
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,380
Gee, Sengoku.

447
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:15,840
Just get it off your chest

448
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:16,260
and tell him

449
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,420
you've been dating for a while.

450
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:18,760
Will it be the loose cannon?

451
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,260
How's Ayasaki been?

452
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:21,640
You see her today at school?

453
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:22,900
Oh, I forgot.

454
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:24,760
Or the oblivious time bomb.

455
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:26,160
The time bomb

456
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,540
is the real danger here.

457
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:28,320
That's you!

458
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:29,920
But I'm human.

459
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:31,780
He's a freaking teenager.

460
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:32,840
Falling in love

461
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:33,980
is kind of what they do.

462
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:35,540
Isn't it a little excessive

463
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:37,100
to say you can't date at all?

464
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,360
This could work.

465
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:39,600
A peaceful resolution!

466
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:41,300
Mind your business.

467
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:42,360
Our family affairs

468
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,560
have nothing to do with you.

469
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:44,460
Why latch into

470
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:46,040
those outdated beliefs, Grandpa?

471
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,300
It ain't hip, yo.

472
00:18:47,380 --> 00:18:48,660
We're parents, not hippies.

473
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,140
And did you actually bring me here

474
00:18:50,140 --> 00:18:50,980
in my personal time

475
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:51,520
to lecture me

476
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:52,180
when I'm older

477
00:18:52,180 --> 00:18:53,240
and smarter than you are?

478
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,520
You forget who brought you bread

479
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:55,680
that time you left your lunch.

480
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:56,180
You mean the bread

481
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:57,080
that costs 80 yen?

482
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:57,900
You tricked me

483
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:58,920
and said it costs 100.

484
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,560
I want my 20 yen!

485
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:02,180
They completely veered off topic.

486
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,180
It's almost as if...

487
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:05,780
This isn't an adult conversation.

488
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,780
It's a high school fight.

489
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:11,300
Don't make me tell him, dude.

490
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,460
Remember when you walked

491
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:13,060
through what seemed to be

492
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:13,700
a normal puddle

493
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:14,300
and got soaked up

494
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:15,320
to your knees, my friend?

495
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:16,740
You want the kids to know?

496
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,220
You just told them!

497
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:19,260
Though remind me,

498
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:20,500
which moron arrived at school

499
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:22,000
after all our exams were over?

500
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
It only happened

501
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:23,900
because someone stole

502
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,260
the front wheel of my bike.

503
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:25,740
You should have

504
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:26,740
bought the bike and walked!

505
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:27,640
Good grief.

506
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:28,880
It's like a bad dream,

507
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:29,480
but it's real.

508
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:30,420
Oh, really?

509
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:32,400
This is par for the course for us.

510
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:33,960
Wow, I can tell

511
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:34,920
how close you guys are.

512
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:35,980
Life-long pals.

513
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:38,520
Sengoku and I

514
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,480
are the bestest friends.

515
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:39,920
Ha!

516
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,340
Bestest friends, my ass!

517
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:42,440
I won't ever forget

518
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:43,240
what you did to me

519
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,360
on graduation day.

520
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:45,580
Right as I was giving

521
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:46,080
my speech

522
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,320
as student council president.

523
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:50,720
I know that sneeze was planned!

524
00:19:51,020 --> 00:19:51,860
Don't deny it!

525
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,120
And sneeze

526
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,060
was the student body rep.

527
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,640
Our school had no such rep!

528
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:57,520
Let's circle back

529
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:58,160
to talking about

530
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:59,200
Sengoku's love life.

531
00:19:59,300 --> 00:19:59,860
That was fun.

532
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,700
Oh, boy!

533
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:02,300
I sure wish you'd keep

534
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:02,960
telling stories

535
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:03,980
from the good old days!

536
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,320
Don't laugh off

537
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,160
by humiliation!

538
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:07,520
It seems

539
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:08,940
even years later,

540
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:11,080
the Sengokus

541
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,440
are still at the mercy

542
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,040
of the Hodies.

543
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:13,540
Ha!

544
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:13,580
Ha!

545
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:14,080
Ha!

546
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:14,580
Ha!

547
00:20:14,580 --> 00:20:15,080
Ha!

548
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:15,580
Ha!

549
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:16,080
Ha!

550
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:16,580
Ha!

551
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,080
Ha!

552
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:17,120
Ha!

553
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:17,160
Ha!

554
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:17,300
Ha!

555
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:17,820
Ha!

556
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:20,060
But seriously,

557
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:20,840
a girlfriend

558
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:21,760
isn't a temptation

559
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:22,760
you need right now.

560
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:24,040
Especially if she's

561
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:24,600
anything like

562
00:20:24,600 --> 00:20:25,300
Hori's daughter.

563
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:27,280
It got harder

564
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,000
to tell him.

565
00:20:30,620 --> 00:20:31,220
Imports

566
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:32,540
are like imports

567
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:33,620
because they come

568
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:34,840
into Japan.

569
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:37,500
Hope I can score

570
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:38,380
